        <!-- Footer notes -->
        <mxCell id="footer_notes" value="Why RRF: BM25 and cosine produce non-comparable score scales. Reciprocal Rank Fusion uses ranks (not raw scores), so the two systems can be combined without normalization quirks.&#10;Why one collection per library: keeps the vector space cohesive (clustering, recommendations) and lets users selectively rebuild a single library after a model upgrade.&#10;Cross-language retrieval: e5-large is multilingual, so an English query can match Arabic units.&#10;Permission scope: the API filters hits against library_acl AFTER retrieval — ChromaDB has no ACL." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="qry_section">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="780" width="2280" height="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

